            {
              "id": "SNYK-JS-LODASH-15869625",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Arbitrary Code Injection vulnerability in lodash"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-4800) lodash@4.17.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "* Package Manager: npm\n* Vulnerable module: lodash\n* Introduced through: lab-dom12-server-details@1.0.0 and lodash@4.17.20\n### Detailed paths\n* _Introduced through_: lab-dom12-server-details@1.0.0 › lodash@4.17.20\n# Overview\n[lodash](https://www.npmjs.com/package/lodash) is a modern JavaScript utility library delivering modularity, performance, & extras.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Arbitrary Code Injection due the improper validation of `options.imports` key names in `_.template`. An attacker can execute arbitrary code at template compilation time by injecting malicious expressions. If `Object.prototype` has been polluted, inherited properties may also be copied into the imports object and executed.\r\n\r\n**Notes:**\r\n\r\n1) Version 4.18.0 was intended to fix this vulnerability but it got deprecated due to introducing a breaking [functionality issue](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/issues/6167).\r\n\r\n2) This issue is due to the incomplete fix for [CVE-2021-23337](https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JS-LODASH-1040724).\n# Remediation\nUpgrade `lodash` to version 4.18.1 or higher.\n# References\n- [GitHub Advisory](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/security/advisories/GHSA-r5fr-rjxr-66jc)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/commit/879aaa93132d78c2f8d20c60279da9f8b21576d6)\n- [GitHub Issue](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/issues/6167)\n- [OpenJS Security Advisory](https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html)\n"
              },
